(4859242, 703152, 62027, '<td valign="top">this is not a bad shot! Perhaps re-adjusting the camera focus, and decide whether or not the dragon should be front and center. If the idea is to invoke the idea of "lawn" this one speaks more to the dragon. Maybe offsetting the dragon to another portion of your frame while still focusing on some portion of the grass could create a stronger connection? Rule of Thirds! You have a creative thought here, keep going with it :)</td>', 'this is not a bad shot! Perhaps re-adjusting the camera focus, and decide whether or not the dragon should be front and center. If the idea is to invoke the idea of "lawn" this one speaks more to the dragon. Maybe offsetting the dragon to another portion of your frame while still focusing on some portion of the grass could create a stronger connection? Rule of Thirds! You have a creative thought here, keep going with it :)', '2008-08-02 12:54:16.000000', NULL, 1),
